<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Faithfulness in <span id="A2.T3.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conflicting</span> and <span id="A2.T3.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Double-Conflicting</span> contexts for two models on two datasets (short-context: World Capital, long-context: Fakepedia). Higher AOPC<math id="A2.T3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{comp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{comp}}</annotation></semantics></math>, lower AOPC<math id="A2.T3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{suff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>suff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{suff}}</annotation></semantics></math> is better. Best entries are <span id="A2.T3.20" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underlined</span> for comprehensiveness and <span id="A2.T3.21" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span> for sufficiency. MechLight and FA are the best AOPC<math id="A2.T3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{suff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>suff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{suff}}</annotation></semantics></math>; ATTN is the best for AOPC<math id="A2.T3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{comp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{comp}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Conflicting setup.</figcaption>
</figure>
